WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:04.630
If the trip home takes
39 minutes, at what time

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:06.600
does Chris have
to leave in order

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:09.465
to be home by a
quarter after 6:00?

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:14.740
So let's draw a time
line and then think

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:16.779
about what has to happen here.

00:00:16.779 --> 00:00:18.570
This is at least how
I need to visualize it

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:20.420
in order to solve this problem.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:23.060
And I'm going to do the hours
before 6:00 and after 6:00.

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:25.170
So I'll start at 5:00 and
I'll go up to 7:00 just

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:27.516
to make sure that we
capture everything.

00:00:27.516 --> 00:00:29.140
I can draw a straighter
line than that,

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:31.810
so let me draw it a
little bit straighter.

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:34.420
Still not perfect,
but it'll do the job.

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:37.280
So let's say that
this is 5 o'clock.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:40.780
This is 6 o'clock.

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:43.510
And they don't specify
whether it's AM or PM.

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:44.805
And this is 7 o'clock.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:51.020
They tell us he has to be
home by a quarter after 6:00.

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:53.310
So what is a quarter after 6:00?

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:56.060
Well, it's going to be a
quarter of the way between 6

00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:57.320
and 7 o'clock.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:01.010
So this would be half of the
way between 6 and 7 o'clock.

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:03.220
And then a quarter
would be half of that.

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:05.640
So this would be a
quarter after 6:00.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:09.460
And if we wanted to specify
what time a quarter after 6:00

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:12.690
is, a quarter of the way
between 6:00 and 7:00,

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:15.300
we know there are 60
minutes in an hour.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:16.990
So this distance is 60 minutes.

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:19.890
A quarter of 60 is 15 minutes.

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:23.240
So this time right
over here is 6:15.

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:25.600
And that's when
Chris has to be home.

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:29.180
Now, they tell us that the
trip home takes 39 minutes.

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:34.890
So he would have to have left
39 minutes before this in order

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:37.610
to get home at 6:15.

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:41.660
So let's go 39 minutes
before this to figure out

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:43.620
the time that he would
have to leave in order

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:45.600
to be home by 6:15.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:52.780
So what is 39
minutes before 6:15?

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:54.930
Now, the way my
brain processes it,

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:57.990
I like to think about,
well, how much time

00:01:57.990 --> 00:02:00.050
does it take to get to the hour?

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:01.600
And then how much
time do you have

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:04.430
left to go before the hour?

00:02:04.430 --> 00:02:08.880
So this part right over
here is 15 minutes.

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:13.370
If you go back 15 minutes
from 6:15 and go to 6 o'clock,

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:15.460
that was 15 minutes.

00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:19.440
So we've already gone 15 minutes
back if we go to 6 o'clock.

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:22.350
And then how many minutes
do we have left to go back?

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:24.860
Well, we went 15 of the 39.

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:30.080
39 minus 15 is 24.

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:33.980
So we have to go another
24 minutes before the hour.

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:47.890
So this time right over here
is 24 minutes before 6 o'clock.

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:50.140
And once again, the way we
figured it out, well, look.

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:52.620
Going from 6:15, if
you go 15 minutes back,

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:54.050
you get to 6 o'clock.

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:56.390
We have to go 39,
so we have 24 left.

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:59.260
So then we have to go 24
minutes before 6 o'clock.

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:01.230
But 24 minutes before
6 o'clock would

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:04.011
be how many minutes
after 5 o'clock?

00:03:04.011 --> 00:03:05.510
Well, once again,
we know that there

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:07.610
are 60 minutes in an hour.

00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:10.000
So what's 60 minus 24?

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:11.440
Let me do it right over here.

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:18.760
So 60 minus 24 is equal to 36.

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:20.690
And you could either
do that in your head.

00:03:20.690 --> 00:03:23.530
Or you could say, hey, look,
I could maybe borrow here.

00:03:23.530 --> 00:03:24.830
This is a 10.

00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:26.070
This is a 5 for a regroup.

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:27.270
10 minus 4 is 6.

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:29.230
5 minus 2 is 3.

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:37.560
The way my brain does it is
I say, oh, well, 60 minus 20

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:39.120
would get me to 40.

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:42.110
And then I need to subtract
another 4 more to get to 36.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:45.610
But either way, if we're talking
about 24 minutes before 6

00:03:45.610 --> 00:03:54.800
o'clock, that's the equivalent
to 36 minutes after 5 o'clock.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:57.820
So this time right
over here is 5:36.

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:02.290
So when they say,
what time does Chris

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:05.560
have to leave in order to be
home by a quarter after 6:00?

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:07.110
5:36.

